Subject: Cantor Public Procedure Machine Schema Semantic Refinement

@ [refinement_uuid] 1430eadc-5e07-4a03-8f66-7d9c6dff7e8e

& [MachineSchema] means syntax contract
  + a closed deterministic description of JSON names, types, required properties, nullability, enum values, array and map shape, numeric bounds, and definitions
  - never: truth, trust, signature, semantic validity, authority, consent, safety, or fitness

& [TypeFingerprint] means implementation binding
  + stable identity and content digest over one exported transport form's canonical schema
  + detects schema drift but does not prove compiler or executable integrity

& [SchemaBundle] means one compatible family
  + exact dialect, profile, operation schemas, response schemas, shared definitions, type fingerprints, generator identity, source revision, residual registry, and bundle digest

& [SemanticResidual] means post-schema obligation
  + condition intentionally not represented as sufficient JSON syntax
  + examples are digest recomputation, referential integrity, source binding, policy subset, causal order, replay equality, authorship evidence, and admission

& [ProviderProjection] means lossy or exact mapping
  + derives one provider's supported tool schema from the canonical bundle
  + declares every weakened, omitted, rewritten, or externally enforced constraint
  + cannot amend canonical meaning

& [Compatibility] has explicit kinds
  + identical means canonical schema bytes equal
  + backward_input_compatible means every old valid syntax remains valid under the new input schema
  + forward_output_compatible means old consumers can accept every new output shape
  + breaking means neither claim is proven
  + semantic compatibility is separately evaluated by Cantor validators
